laurel 3081: LAUREL SWAP, part 2: the iPhone swap path and sizes on this kernel. [V phone 06:34:54, 3080 kernel] "LAUREL SWAP: off: already with swap: mode 0x4 stays": the Mi A3 kernel is built for the macOS platform (XNU_SDK MacOSX, XNU_TARGET_OS_OSX), so vm_compressor_mode was VM_PAGER_COMPRESSOR_WITH_SWAP from the start, with macOS values: swap files in /System/Volumes/VM (no such directory on the root: no file was ever made, compressor only), 256 MiB to 1 GiB each, up to 100 (VM_MAX_SWAP_FILE_NUM). On ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET the three blocks take the !XNU_TARGET_OS_OSX values: /private/var/vm/swapfileN, 64 to 128 MiB each, at most 5 (640 MiB). The on line now prints when the mode has swap (changed or not), with the path and the limit: "LAUREL SWAP: on: already with swap: mode 0x4: compressed pages go to /private/var/vm/swapfileN, at most 5 x 128 MiB, 4078 MiB RAM". Both kernels (xnu-12377: the header is vm_compressor_backing_store_internal.h with other context: series rule drop_file + post/9025 for the header; the .c hunk applies). docs/laurel_sprout/memory.md.

diff -ruN a/osfmk/vm/laurel_swap.c b/osfmk/vm/laurel_swap.c
--- a/osfmk/vm/laurel_swap.c	2026-11-07 06:38:52.381104078 +0530
+++ b/osfmk/vm/laurel_swap.c	2026-11-07 06:38:52.381216556 +0530
@@ -16,6 +16,7 @@
